      "findings": [
        {
          "area": "First eligible weakspot and restart behavior",
          "result": "accepted",
          "detail": "The first weakspot event initializes the blessing counter to 1 without reducing Peril. A later eligible weakspot event with combo_count > 0 reduces Peril. Body-hit and miss events fail the weakspot check before proc_func, so they do not execute the counter-reset branch. The restart example correctly conditions reinitialization on game combo_count having returned to 0."
        },
        {
          "area": "Multi-target sweep behavior",
          "result": "accepted",
          "detail": "ActionSweep OR-aggregates weakspot results across targets and emits one on_sweep_finish event per completed sweep. The examples correctly state that multiple weakspot targets in one swing still allow only one reduction."
        },
        {
          "area": "Peril arithmetic",
          "result": "accepted",
          "detail": "Tier values 0.02/0.03/0.04/0.05 are represented as 2/3/4/5 percentage points of the full gauge. The 40% to 35% example, max(0, 3%-5pp)=0% lower-bound example, and contrast with proportional multiplication are correct."
        },
        {
          "area": "Body hit between weakspot hits",
          "result": "accepted",
          "detail": "The example explicitly assumes the game combo remains active. A body-hit sweep does not pass the weakspot check and therefore does not clear the blessing counter; a subsequent weakspot event can continue the count while combo_count remains positive."
        },
        {
          "area": "Switching and return",
          "result": "accepted",
          "detail": "Switching away suppresses proc processing through the held-slot condition, while the on_equip buff and its internal counter remain. Returning does not itself vent Peril; if combo_count has reset to 0, the next weakspot event only starts the counter again. The current player text states this condition and does not promise immediate reduction."
        },
        {
          "area": "0.2-second combo reset",
          "result": "accepted",
          "detail": "The text correctly describes the default combo timeout as idle time after an ended, non-looping action, not a timer since the last weakspot hit. The reset is evaluated only when combo_count is positive; the three Force Sword templates do not override the default duration."
        },
        {
          "area": "Rules classifications",
          "result": "accepted",
          "detail": "The table uses the workflow classifications consistently: the RAW Traditional Chinese direction is an explicit contradiction; numerical implementation details omitted from the description are marked as not covered; the tier values align with the tooltip/code."
        }
      ],
